# Study loading overlay

Protected study UI is wrapped by `StudyLoadingProvider` ([`components/study/study-loading-provider.tsx`](components/study/study-loading-provider.tsx)). Use the shared overlay ([`StudyLoadingOverlay`](components/study/study-loading-overlay.tsx)) for **blocking** client API work — anything the user must wait on before continuing (initial page load, save, retry, submit).

The overlay **is** the loader. Never add a second spinner (`StudyLoader`, “Loading…” copy, section loaders) for the same wait.

## Soft Nav (in-app link / router transitions)

Use [`StudyNavLink`](components/study/study-nav-link.tsx) instead of raw `next/link`, and [`useStudyRouter`](hooks/use-study-router.ts) instead of bare `router.push` / `replace`, inside the study shell. Soft Nav **holds** the shared overlay; route change **releases** that hold. [`StudyControlLink`](components/study/study-button.tsx) already wraps `StudyNavLink`.

Do **not** call `run()` for Soft Nav alone — `run()` releases in `finally` before the route settles. Prefer Soft Nav hold, or `hold('soft-nav')` then navigate.

## One overlay only

There is a single viewport portal in [`StudyLoadingProvider`](components/study/study-loading-provider.tsx). Overlapping waits use **holds** (`soft-nav`, `route`, `manual`, …) so Soft Nav → page boot never mounts a second overlay or swaps copy mid-wait.

Route boots must use [`StudyRouteLoading`](components/study/study-route-loading.tsx) / [`useStudyRouteLoading`](hooks/use-study-route-loading.ts) with [`STUDY_ROUTE_LOADING_LABEL`](lib/study/loading.ts). Do **not** render another viewport `StudyLoadingOverlay` beside the provider. Reserve custom labels for discrete actions (save, submit, start test).

## Two valid ways to open it

### 1. Declarative (preferred for initial / route loading)

Tie `open` to loading UI state so the overlay is present on the **first render** (and SSR), not after a `useEffect`:

```tsx
if (authStatus === "loading" || profileStatus === "loading") {
  return (
    <>
      <Header />
      <StudyLoadingOverlay open scope="viewport" label={STUDY_ROUTE_LOADING_LABEL} />
    </>
  );
}
```

Do **not** also call `show()` / `run()` for that same wait (double overlay).

### 2. Imperative `run()` (saves / retries while the page is already visible)

```tsx
const studyLoading = useStudyLoadingOverlay();

await studyLoading.run(
  () => updateMyProfile(payload),
  { label: "Saving your details..." }
);
```

Call `run` from event handlers. Do not assign `ref.current` during render. For initial route loads, prefer declarative `open` so the overlay paints before effects run.

## Do not overlay

- **Background** work (prefetch, silent revalidate, analytics, fire-and-forget).
- Pure local state with no network.
- Server Components / route handlers.

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — empty shell first; show() only in useEffect (flash)
useEffect(() => {
  studyLoading.show({ label: "Loading..." });
  void load();
}, []);
if (loading) return <Header />; // no overlay in the tree

// ❌ BAD — overlay + second StudyLoader
<>
  <StudyLoadingOverlay open />
  <StudyLoader label="Loading..." />
</>

// ✅ GOOD — overlay open on the loading render
if (loading) {
  return (
    <>
      <Header />
      <StudyLoadingOverlay open label={STUDY_ROUTE_LOADING_LABEL} />
    </>
  );
}
```
